        "section": [
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">COPD exacerbation, treated with bronchodilators and steroids</div>"
            },
            "code": {
              "coding": [
                {
                  "code": "67781-5",
                  "system": "http://loinc.org",
                  "display": "Summarization of encounter note"
                }
              ]
            },
            "title": "Synthesis"
          },
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the recent hospital admission of your 78-year-old female patient, who presented with an acute exacerbation of her known chronic obstructive pulmonary disease. On admission, she displayed marked dyspnoea, increased sputum production, and reduced oxygen saturation. Chest X-ray confirmed hyperinflation without consolidation. Arterial blood gas analysis revealed hypoxaemia with mild hypercapnia. Blood tests showed elevated inflammatory markers. She was promptly commenced on supplemental oxygen, nebulised bronchodilators, and a course of systemic corticosteroids. Continuous pulse oximetry monitoring was maintained throughout. Her respiratory status improved steadily, and she was discharged in a stable condition. I recommend continued follow-up for her COPD management and review of her inhaler technique and adherence. Please do not hesitate to contact me should you require further information.</div>"
            },
            "code": {
              "coding": [
